\section{CONCLUSION}
This study found that informal carers of people with AD in the early stage of the disease can learn validation therapy skills, but there needs to be a strong focus during training on helping carers recognize when their own emotional needs may need attention, so that they can be supported to avoid becoming distressed by the caregiving experience. There also needs to be more information about where carers can go for help and support during training sessions, as well as more support for them after they complete training in validation therapy skills.

